format: loopthing/container-v0.4
title: The Missing Artifact
kind: rich-ai-work-container
created: 2026-04-29T07:18:00Z
entry: Prompts/Master Prompt.md
origin: OpenAI Codex hackathon demo
mimetype: application/vnd.loopthing+zip

summary:
  A .loopthing is a rich portable file for AI work: prompts, follow-ups,
  discarded ideas, rough drafts, generated explainers, screenshots, docs,
  slides, prototypes, and code that show how an idea arrived.

generator:
  input: messy AI chat session
  output: net new artifacts and explainers for sharing the work
  promise: make the creator look clear, deliberate, intelligent, and easy to learn from

lineage:
  - Began as a static OpenAI Codex hackathon viewer.
  - Used OpenClaw as the first source artifact.
  - Tried a GitHub repo input direction.
  - Killed "LoopThing a repo" because the repo is not the thinking process.
  - Became a portable rich-file container for AI work.
  - Added generated explainers as a core function, not a side effect.

principles:
  - One .loopthing file is the shareable container.
  - loopthing-source/ is only the unpacked editing source.
  - Prompts are the canonical spine.
  - The container generates context artifacts, not just summaries.
  - Discarded ideas make the sharer look clearer, not messier.
  - Screenshots, docs, slides, prototypes, and code travel with the thought process.

